      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8.1 Important Facts about Goa — Quick Reference"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Goa was liberated from 451 years of Portuguese rule on December 19, 1961, through Operation Vijay.",
        "It was granted full statehood on May 30, 1987, becoming the 25th state of the Republic of India.",
        "Goa is currently the only Indian state with an active Uniform Civil Code (UCC) derived from the Portuguese Civil Code of 1867.",
        "Major recent infrastructure milestones include the commissioning of the new greenfield Manohar International Airport at Mopa.",
        "The state's rail connectivity relies heavily on the Konkan Railway network and the South Western Railway."
      ],
      "id": "jowces6"
    },
